# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings. /usr/bin/env reads the shebang
# literally, so a CRLF shebang fails with: bash\r: No such file or directory.
#
# core.autocrlf=true with no .gitattributes re-encoded every text file to CRLF
# on export, which is what broke deploy/deploy.sh on the first scp-based deploy.
*.sh text eol=lf
